'''The Viral Fever''', abbreviated to '''TVF''', is an Indian [[video on demand]] and [[over-the-top media service]] and [[YouTube]] channel started by TVF Media Labs in 2010, and currently owned and operated by Contagious Online Media Network Private Limited.<ref>{{cite web|title=The new kings of satire|url=https://www.outlookbusiness.com/enterprise/emerging-business/the-new-kings-of-satire-623|publisher=Outlook Business|date=17 April 2015|access-date=2017-11-24|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170419230905/http://www.outlookbusiness.com/enterprise/emerging-business/the-new-kings-of-satire-623|archive-date=2017-04-19|url-status=live}}</ref> According to the founder [[Arunabh Kumar]], the thought behind starting TVF was to reach out to the younger generation who seldom watch television entertainment.<ref name=":0">{{cite news|title=Entertainment channel for youth|url=http://economictimes.indiatimes.com/magazines/panache/this-iit-kharagpur-alumnus-is-the-brain-behind-the-viral-fever-media/articleshow/46142385.cms|access-date=16 March 2015|work=Economic Times India|date=6 February 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150927210434/http://economictimes.indiatimes.com/magazines/panache/this-iit-kharagpur-alumnus-is-the-brain-behind-the-viral-fever-media/articleshow/46142385.cms|archive-date=2015-09-27|url-status=live|last1=Saxena |first1=Aditi }}</ref>

The Viral Fever was one of the early arrivals on the Indian digital entertainment segment with videos covering a range of topics on Indian politics, movies, lifestyle, and emerging social concepts.<ref>{{cite web|title=Entertainment Network for serious laughter|url=http://www.newindianexpress.com/education/edex/Lessons-in-Laughter/2014/04/21/article2170443.ece|access-date=16 March 2015|work=New Indian Express|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150218110059/http://www.newindianexpress.com/education/edex/Lessons-in-Laughter/2014/04/21/article2170443.ece|archive-date=2015-02-18|url-status=dead}}</ref> The Viral Fever was the pioneer of [[web series]] in India with cult hits like ''[[Permanent Roommates]]'', ''Hostel Daze, [[TVF Pitchers]]'' and ''[[TVF Tripling]]''.

The company runs the app and website TVFPlay to host their videos. TVF conceptualised the idea of promoting movies through the creation and distribution of original digital content. The Ishq Wala song series is one such venture.<ref>{{cite web|title=Bollywood Movies promo through songs|url=http://www.telegraphindia.com/1121106/jsp/entertainment/story_16162975.jsp|access-date=16 March 2015|work=Telegraph India|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150402175835/http://www.telegraphindia.com/1121106/jsp/entertainment/story_16162975.jsp|archive-date=2015-04-02|url-status=dead}}</ref>

Their first web series, ''Permanent Roommates'', debuted in 2014.<ref name=tvfpr>{{cite web|url=http://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/the-webstars/|title=Year 2015: When the web series formula arrived in India|date=30 December 2015|publisher=Indian Express|first=Somya|last=Lakhani|access-date=2016-01-14|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160104055347/http://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/the-webstars/|archive-date=2016-01-04|url-status=live}}</ref> It was the second most-viewed long-form web series in the world by June 2015.<ref name=tvfpr1>{{cite web|url=http://www.thehindu.com/features/metroplus/permanent-roommates-going-the-web-way/article7329851.ece|title=Permanent Roommates: Going the web way|work=The Hindu|access-date=30 December 2015|date=18 June 2015|first=Priyanka|last=Parthasarathi|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170101232026/http://www.thehindu.com/features/metroplus/permanent-roommates-going-the-web-way/article7329851.ece|archive-date=2017-01-01|url-status=live}}</ref> A second original series titled ''TVF Pitchers'' was released in June 2015. It portrays engineers at different companies who quit their jobs to create a [[startup company]].<ref name=tvfpitchers>{{cite web|url=http://www.firstpost.com/bollywood/tvf-pitchers-review-just-like-beer-this-intelligent-web-show-flows-freely-2416458.html|title=TVF 'Pitchers' ii review: Just like beer, this intelligent web series flows freely|publisher=First Post|date=2 September 2015|first=Manas|last=Mitul|access-date=2016-01-14|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151230234750/http://www.firstpost.com/bollywood/tvf-pitchers-review-just-like-beer-this-intelligent-web-show-flows-freely-2416458.html|archive-date=2015-12-30|url-status=live}}</ref> Owing to its growing popularity, with both ''TVF Pitchers'' and ''Permanent Roommates'' being watched by millions around the globe, the company received $10 million in funding from [[Tiger Global]] in February 2016.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.venturegali.com/2016/02/17/online-videos-creator-tvf-receive-10-million-in-funding-from-tiger-global | title=Online Videos creator TVF receives $10 million in funding from Tiger Global | publisher=Venture Gali | date=17 February 2016 | access-date=18 February 2016 | author=Chopra, Vidit | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160221025930/http://www.venturegali.com/2016/02/17/online-videos-creator-tvf-receive-10-million-in-funding-from-tiger-global | archive-date=2016-02-21 | url-status=usurped }}</ref>

==Background==

===Early days===
After graduating from [[Indian Institute of Technology Kharagpur|IIT Kharagpur]], [[Arunabh Kumar]] quit his job as a consultant for [[Red Chillies Entertainment]] to try his hand at production jobs, including assisting [[Farah Khan]] on ''[[Om Shanti Om]]''.<ref name="Saxena">{{Cite news|url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/magazines/panache/this-iit-kharagpur-alumnus-is-the-brain-behind-the-viral-fever-media/articleshow/46142385.cms|title=This IIT Kharagpur alumnus is the brain behind The Viral Fever Media|last=Saxena|first=Aditi|date=2015-02-06|work=The Economic Times|access-date=2018-02-25|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180225205956/https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/magazines/panache/this-iit-kharagpur-alumnus-is-the-brain-behind-the-viral-fever-media/articleshow/46142385.cms|archive-date=2018-02-25|url-status=live}}</ref>

Kumar, along with long-time friends and fellow [[Indian Institutes of Technology|IIT]] alumni, Amit Golani, and [[Biswapati Sarkar]] began pitching shows targeting young people to [[MTV]].<ref name="Saxena"/> Faced with rejection, The Viral Fever was founded when the group came together and released a video titled Rowdies on YouTube starring Deepak Kumar Mishra and [[Naveen Kasturia]]. The runaway success of the video prompted Arunabh to create the YouTube-focused video company, The Viral Fever, in 2012.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.livemint.com/Leisure/pPNZeU4jPzUj1jU99aL8NN/How-The-Viral-Fever-went-viral.html|title=How The Viral Fever went viral|last=Jhunjhunwala|first=Udita|date=2016-04-29|work=livemint.com/|access-date=2018-02-25|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180225210428/http://www.livemint.com/Leisure/pPNZeU4jPzUj1jU99aL8NN/How-The-Viral-Fever-went-viral.html|archive-date=2018-02-25|url-status=live}}</ref>

After a few years of creating "viral videos", The Viral Fever released India's first web series, ''[[Permanent Roommates]]'', in 2014.<ref name=":1">{{Cite news |url=http://www.firstpost.com/entertainment/tvf-pitchers-review-just-like-beer-this-intelligent-web-show-flows-freely-2416458.html |title=TVF 'Pitchers' review: Just like beer, this intelligent web series flows freely |work=Firstpost |access-date=2018-02-25 |language=en-US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180220195817/http://www.firstpost.com/entertainment/tvf-pitchers-review-just-like-beer-this-intelligent-web-show-flows-freely-2416458.html |archive-date=2018-02-20 |url-status=live}}</ref>

TVF debuted their own platform, TVFPlay, releasing the final two episodes of ''Pitchers''. The platform saw 10 lakh (1 million) hits in the first two days and crashed for 3 hours. In early 2016, venture capital firm [[Tiger Management|Tiger Global]] invested $10 million into TVF, acquiring a 20% stake in the company.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.livemint.com/Companies/3TwExKIWy3bPwVZS4APOjM/Tiger-Global-invests-10-million-in-online-videos-creator-Th.html|title=Tiger Global invests $10 million in online videos creator The Viral Fever|last=Dhanjal|first=Swaraj Singh|date=2016-02-17|work=livemint.com/|access-date=2018-02-25|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180218144321/http://www.livemint.com/Companies/3TwExKIWy3bPwVZS4APOjM/Tiger-Global-invests-10-million-in-online-videos-creator-Th.html|archive-date=2018-02-18|url-status=live}}</ref> 

==Content==
{{Main|List of productions by The Viral Fever}}

===''The Making Of...'' (2014)===
Focused on the making of entertainment products in India, ranging from a blockbuster movie to a decade long TV soap. The first season of ''The Making Of...'' comprised five episodes, with a standalone episode released for Season 2 in 2016.<ref>https://tvfplay.com/category/1/series/(Sudhanshu Suman)</ref>

===''Permanent Roommates'' (since 2014)===
{{Main|Permanent Roommates}}

''[[Permanent Roommates]]'' is an Indian [[web series]] created by TVF and [[Biswapati Sarkar]]. This series revolves around a young couple, Tanya and Mikesh, who after being in a long-distance relationship for 3 years, face the prospect of marriage. The first season was released on YouTube on 31 October 2014.<ref name=":1" />

===''Barely Speaking with Arnub'' (since 2014)===
''Barely Speaking with Arnub'' returned for a shortened season two in 2016.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.huffingtonpost.in/2016/07/20/the-viral-fevers-barely-speaking-with-arnub-is-returning-with_a_21435511/|title=The Viral Fever's 'Barely Speaking With Arnub' Is Returning With Season 2|date=2016-07-20|work=Huffington Post India|access-date=2018-02-25|language=en-IN|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180225205901/http://www.huffingtonpost.in/2016/07/20/the-viral-fevers-barely-speaking-with-arnub-is-returning-with_a_21435511/|archive-date=2018-02-25|url-status=live}}</ref> The show has been on hold as writer Biswapati Sarkar focuses on writing web series including the sequel to ''TVF Pitchers''.{{fact|date=October 2025}}

===''TVF Pitchers'' (2015-present)===
{{Main|TVF Pitchers}}

''[[TVF Pitchers]]'' is an Indian web series created by TVF and developed by Arunabh Kumar single-handedly with assisting efforts from others. The first season consists of five episodes and premiered online on TVFPlay on 10 June 2015. A week later, on 17 June, it premiered on YouTube. The season finale premiered on TVFPlay on 30 August 2015. It follows four friends, Naveen, Jitu, Yogi and Mandal, who quit their jobs in order to develop their own [[Startup company|start-up company]].

In 2016, TVF announced December 2017 as the projected release of Season 2 of ''Pitchers'' with the last scene of ''Permanent Roommates'', but it failed to materialise later. Later, TVF hinted at the release of the second season of ''[[TVF Pitchers]]'' by uploading a scene in their YouTube video "[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OPQDCTRbymU Shows From The House Of TVF | 2021]".<ref>{{Cite web|title=TVF teases 'Pitchers' Season 2, Twitter says 'here comes the hope!'|url=https://www.freepressjournal.in/entertainment/tvf-teases-pitchers-season-2-twitter-says-here-comes-the-hope|access-date=2021-03-10|website=[[Free Press Journal]]}}</ref>

===''TVF Tripling'' (2016–2022)===
{{Main|TVF Tripling}}

''[[TVF Tripling]]'' is an Asian television award-winning Indian web series created by TVF.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Lakhani|first1=Somya|title=Sibling revelry - Why watching TVF Tripling is so much fun|url=http://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/entertainment-others/the-viral-fever-tvf-tripling-road-trip-sibling-revelry-3033298/|access-date=13 October 2016|publisher=The Indian Express|date=16 September 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161013152417/http://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/entertainment-others/the-viral-fever-tvf-tripling-road-trip-sibling-revelry-3033298/|archive-date=2016-10-13|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.thedigitalhash.com/tvf-asian-television-awards-tripling/|title=TVF wins big at 22nd Asian Television Awards with Tripling TheDigitalHash|last=admin|date=2017-12-06|work=The Digital Hash|access-date=2018-02-25|language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180225205851/https://www.thedigitalhash.com/tvf-asian-television-awards-tripling/|archive-date=2018-02-25|url-status=usurped}}</ref> It traces the story of three siblings Chandan, Chanchal & Chitvan. Together they start a hilarious journey, to find themselves and their relations. Starring Sumeet Vyas, [[Maanvi Gagroo]] and [[Amol Parashar]], and written by Sumeet Vyas and Akarsh Khurana, along with some other contributions, the series has won several awards, including a Kyoorius Blue Elephant. TVF partnered with Tata Motors for the project to promote the newly launched Tata Tiago. ''TVF'' ''Tripling'' was recognised as one of the best web-series of 2016 and is a benchmark of success in Indian branded content.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/magazines/brand-equity/how-auto-brands-have-taken-unconventional-routes-for-marketing-their-produts/articleshow/55958120.cms|title=How auto brands have taken unconventional routes for marketing their {{Sic|produ|ts|hide=y}}|last=Balakrishnan|first=Ravi|date=2016-12-13|work=The Economic Times|access-date=2018-02-25|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180225210129/https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/magazines/brand-equity/how-auto-brands-have-taken-unconventional-routes-for-marketing-their-produts/articleshow/55958120.cms|archive-date=2018-02-25|url-status=live}}</ref> The second season of the series was released on 5 April 2019 aired through [[SonyLIV]], followed by the third season which premiered on 21 October 2022, as a [[ZEE5]] exclusive.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://news.abplive.com/entertainment/web-series/zee5-partners-with-tvf-the-viral-fever-announces-pitchers-season-2-tripling-season-3-humorously-yours-season-3-1463539|title=OTT Platform ZEE5 Partners With TVF; Announces 'Pitchers S2', 'Humorously Yours S3' And Others|last=Kushwah|first=Aakash|date=2023-03-23|work=ABP News Bureau|access-date=2021-06-04}}</ref>
===''Tech Conversations With Dad'' (since 2014)===
An ongoing TVF series about Jeetu ([[Jitendra Kumar]]) and his conversations with his father ([[Gajraj Rao]]),<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.ndtv.com/offbeat/when-parents-just-dont-get-it-a-father-son-tech-talk-is-ultimate-facepalm-654894|title=When Parents Just Don't Get it: A Father-Son Tech Talk is Ultimate Facepalm|work=NDTV.com|access-date=2018-02-25|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180225205758/https://www.ndtv.com/offbeat/when-parents-just-dont-get-it-a-father-son-tech-talk-is-ultimate-facepalm-654894|archive-date=2018-02-25|url-status=live}}</ref> often about technology, relationships, and families in India. This is TVF's longest-running digital title with 10 videos in 4 years.

===''Humorously Yours'' (since 2016)===
Long-time TVF writer, and stand-up comic [[Vipul Goyal]] featured in a semi-autobiographical story about the life of a stand-up comic. The show furthered TVF's reputation for story-telling in the Indian context.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.thequint.com/entertainment/tvf-has-another-winner-on-its-plate-with-humorously-yours-with-vipul-goyal-in-the-lead|title=Review: TVF Has Another Winner With 'Humorously Yours'|work=The Quint|access-date=2018-02-25|language=en|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180226032108/https://www.thequint.com/entertainment/tvf-has-another-winner-on-its-plate-with-humorously-yours-with-vipul-goyal-in-the-lead|archive-date=2018-02-26|url-status=live}}</ref> ''Humorously Yours'' was renewed for a second season, released in 2019. The show returned for a third season as a part of [[ZEE5]] original programming. It premiered in December 2023.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/web-series/news/hindi/humorously-yours-season-3-to-be-out-on-this-date/articleshow/106148753.cms?from=mdr|title='Humorously Yours' season 3 to be out on this date |work=The Times of India |access-date=2023-02-07|language=en}}</ref>

===''F.A.T.H.E.R.S.'' (2017)===
A ''Tech Conversations with Dad'' spin-off, ''Fathers'' features three veterans of the Indian television screen, Brijendra Kala, Gajraj Rao, and Atul Srivastava, playing three fathers trying to keep up with the times.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/tv/news/hindi/tvf-just-released-the-teaser-for-their-new-series-f-a-t-h-e-r-s-and-its-totally-awesome/articleshow/56740445.cms|title=TVF just released the teaser for their new series F.A.T.H.E.R.S. and it's totally awesome|newspaper=The Times of India|access-date=2017-01-24|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170125081130/http://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/tv/news/hindi/tvf-just-released-the-teaser-for-their-new-series-f-a-t-h-e-r-s-and-its-totally-awesome/articleshow/56740445.cms|archive-date=2017-01-25|url-status=live}}</ref>

===''Bachelors'' (since 2016)===
''Bachelors'' is a show about four bachelors who live together and encounter hilarious situations as they face the world after college. In 2016, TVF released a pilot episode of ''Bachelors'', featuring popular YouTube star [[Bhuvan Bam]]. The success of the pilot led to a 4-episode extension with Bam and over 25 million views. Bachelors was picked up for Season 2, released in late 2017, with Jitendra Kumar replacing Bhuvan Bam as the lead. Season 2 has also crossed 25 million views since release and was listed among the best web-series of 2017 by ''[[FilmCompanion]]''<ref>[https://www.filmcompanion.in/features/indepth-stories/streaming/top-5-web-shows-of-2017-ranked FilmCompanion]</ref> and ''[[The Indian Express]]''<ref>{{Cite web |date=2017-12-19 |title=Best Indian Web Series of 2017: Bose Dead/Alive, Inside Edge and Bachelors Season 2 find place in list |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/television/best-indian-web-series-2017-4986817/ |access-date=2026-03-21 |website=The Indian Express |language=en}}</ref>, and was applauded by various sects of audience for its satirical timing, and spoofs of popular Bollywood movies such as [[Dangal (2016 film)|''Dangal'']], [[Bahubali (film)|''Bahubali'']] and ''[[Chak De! India]]'' among many others.

===''The Aam Aadmi Family'' (2016)===
{{Main|The Aam Aadmi Family}}

''[[The Aam Aadmi Family]]'' is a project released from TVF's sister channel The Timeliners. It is an album of moments from the life of a middle-class family based in Delhi. It has garnered an average of 8 million views across 3 seasons.{{citation needed|date=February 2021}}

===''Flames'' (2018)===
[[Flames (web series)|''Flames'']] is another project from TVF's sister channel The Timeliners. It is the story of a young romance unfolding as a chemical reaction. Studious Rajat falls for Ishita, the new girl in the tuition. Rajat's friends, Pandey & Anusha's friendship is beginning to turn into a relationship. The equations of friendships evolve in the first season of this teenage romance. This series has already garnered an average of 5 million views.<ref>{{Cite web|title=aha announces its new original, Tharagathi Gadhi Daati, the official Telugu remake of TVF's hit show FLAMES|date=20 August 2021 |url=https://www.apnnews.com/aha-announces-its-new-original-tharagathi-gadhi-daati-the-official-telugu-remake-of-tvfs-hit-show-flames/|access-date=2021-08-27|language=en-US}}</ref>

===''Yeh Meri Family'' (2018)===
{{Main|Yeh Meri Family}}

''[[Yeh Meri Family]]'' is a mini-series released by TVF. It is about a nuclear-middle-class family living in the height of fad of the 1990s. The story revolves around a 13-year-old boy who is average at academics and is constantly being bullied and blackmailed by his elder brother. It is a mixture of the drama and thrills of being a teenager.

=== ''ImMature'' (2018) ===
{{Main|ImMature}}

''[[ImMature]]'' is a TVF original released in 2019. It stars Omkar Kulkarni, Rashmi Agdekar, Chinmay Chandranushush and Visshesh Tiwari in the lead roles. The show follows a one-conflict-per-episode format that ties into the protagonist Dhruv's larger quest to befriend his love interest Chhavi.<ref>{{cite web|date=23 April 2020|title=ImMature-Best Teenage Web Series|url=https://www.celebswhoop.com/best-web-series-in-hindi/|publisher=CelebsWhoop.com}}</ref>

===''Kota Factory'' (2019-present)===
{{Main|Kota Factory}}

''[[Kota Factory]]'' is a TVF original released in 2019. The series moves around the IIT and Medical entrance coaching industry of Kota, a small town in Rajasthan state of India. It focuses on the life of Vaibhav, who leaves his home town and arrives in Kota to pursue coaching for the preparation of IIT Exam. The series portrays the life of an IIT aspirant during his preparation phase, and also focuses on the different sides of the 'Kota Coaching Industry'. It has been directed by Saurabh Khanna. ''Kota Factory'' is one of the first Indian black-and-white web series on YouTube.

===''Gullak'' (2019-present)===
{{Main|Gullak}}

''Gullak''<ref>{{Cite web|author=Scroll Staff|title='Gullak' trailer: TVF's new web series is about a squabbling family in a North Indian small town|url=https://scroll.in/reel/928062/gullak-trailer-tvfs-new-web-series-is-about-a-squabbling-family-in-a-north-indian-small-town|access-date=2021-08-27|website=Scroll.in|date=23 June 2019 |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=2021-01-27|title=Gullak on SonyLIV belongs to TVF's new brand of soft nostalgia, family binge-watching, and small-town slowness|url=https://www.firstpost.com/entertainment/gullak-on-sonyliv-belongs-to-tvfs-new-brand-of-soft-nostalgia-family-binge-watching-and-small-town-slowness-9224471.html|access-date=2021-08-27|website=Firstpost}}</ref> is a web series that revolves around the life stories of the "Mishra Family", talking tales relatable to a common man's everyday life. The series was created by Shreyansh Pandey. The first season, released on 27 June 2019 on TVF Play and [[SonyLIV]] was directed by the critically acclaimed director of many popular web stories, Amrit Raj Gupta. The second season was directed by Palash Vaswani and was aired on the OTT platform [[SonyLIV]] in 2021. The third season starring the same star-cast released in April 2022 to wide critical acclaim. The show was renewed for a fourth season in 2024 on the OTT platform [[SonyLIV]]. This series features [[Jameel Khan]], [[Geetanjali Kulkarni]], Vaibhav Raj Gupta and [[Shivankit Singh Parihar]].

===''Cubicles'' (2019-present)===
{{main|Cubicles (web series)}}

''Cubicles'' is centered around the life of Piyush, a fresh entrant into the corporate world. The show follows his work life and moments like his very first salary, working weekends, and failures and successes that are a part of anyone's corporate journey. Simultaneously, the series attempts to integrate fundamental concepts of investing and mutual funds into the story. Created by Amit Golani and directed by Chaitanya Kumbhakonum, the series stars Abhishek Chauhan, Nidhi Bisht, Arnav Bhasin, Shivankit Singh Parihar, and Badri Chavan, among others.

===''Hostel Daze'' (2019–2023)===
{{main|Hostel Daze}}

''Hostel Daze'' was created by TVF, and is a compilation of stories depicting the lifestyle and fun of undergraduates who live in a hostel, along with the bullying of seniors being one of their many experiences with the hostel and its residents. The series was released on [[Amazon Prime Video]] on 13 December 2019. The entire series was shot in the campus and hostel of [[Symbiosis International University]], Pune.<ref>{{Citation|title=Hostel Daze (TV Mini-Series 2019– ) - IMDb|url=http://www.imdb.com/title/tt11407524/trivia|access-date=2021-05-20}}</ref> The series was written and created by Saurabh Khanna and Abhishek Yadav, and was directed by Raghav Subbu, critically acclaimed for directing TVF's series [[Kota Factory]]. The series features [[Adarsh Gourav]], Shubham Gaur and LUV in key roles of three freshers, and also casts Nikhil Vijay, Badri Chavan and [[Harsha Chemudu]] among many others.

===''Panchayat'' (2020-present)===
{{Main|Panchayat (TV series)}}

''[[Panchayat (TV series)|Panchayat]]'' is a web series produced by TVF, released on Amazon Prime on 3 April 2020. This critically acclaimed web series revolves around the [[Panchayati raj in India|Panchayat]] of a village called Phulera in [[Ballia district]] of [[Purvanchal|Eastern]] [[Uttar Pradesh]], The series features [[Jitendra Kumar]], who plays the role of a young graduate and the secretary of the Panchayat of the village, who is constantly at war with himself, trying to adapt himself to the lifestyle of the villagers, while keeping his dream of cracking the [[Common Admission Test|CAT]]. The series also features veteran actors like [[Raghubir Yadav]] and [[Neena Gupta]]. The series marked the debut for Chandan Roy as an actor,<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/tv/appreciation-is-bigger-than-awards-panchayat-series-fame-chandan/story-usYbJ5xq5aZinVXqljyI0M.html|title='Appreciation better than any award': Actor Chandan Roy on 'Panchayat' success|date=2020-04-09|website=Hindustan Times|language=en|access-date=2020-04-13}}</ref> playing the role of assistant secretary of the Panchayat. His work is being praised by many cinema critics.<ref>{{Cite news|title=TVF's Panchayat shines at the Flyx Filmfare OTT Awards 2020 - Times of India|url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/tv/spotlight/tvfs-panchayat-shines-at-the-flyx-filmfare-ott-awards-2020/articleshow/80286368.cms|access-date=2021-08-27|website=The Times of India|language=en}}</ref> 

On 28 April 2022, the second season was announced after the completion of the production. <ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.indiatoday.in/binge-watch/story/tvf-s-panchayat-season-2-to-premiere-on-amazon-prime-video-on-may-20-1944548-2022-05-02|title='TVF's Panchayat Season 2 to premiere on Amazon Prime Video on May 20|date=2024-02-05|website=India Today|language=en|access-date=2024-06-02}}</ref> On 2 May 2022, it was announced that the second season will premiere on 20 May 2022. However, Prime Video released all the episodes on 18 May 2022, two days earlier than its actual premiere date. 

Deepak Kumar Mishra revealed to social media that there would be a third season of ''Panchayat''. <ref>{{Cite web|url=https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/web-series/panchayat-director-confirms-season-3-death-scene-7945659/|title=Panchayat director Deepak Kumar Mishra confirms season 3, talks about the death scene: 'We needed something drastic'|date=31 May 2022|website=Indian Express|language=en|access-date=2024-06-02}}</ref> It was later confirmed that season 3 would involve eight episodes and would be released in late 2023 on [[Amazon Prime Video]]. This was further delayed to early 2024. On 28 May 2024, the third season was released.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.business-standard.com/entertainment/panchayat-season-3-now-out-on-prime-here-is-how-you-can-stream-it-for-free-124052800351_1.html/|title=Panchayat Season 3 now out on Prime: Here is how you can stream it for free|date=28 May 2022|website=Indian Express|language=en|access-date=2024-06-02}}</ref>

On 3 April 2025, marking the fifth anniversary of the series, the makers announced that its fourth season will premiere on 24 June 2025.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Panchayat season 4 officially announced: Fans excited as Prime Video announces release date of Jitendra Kumar's cult hit |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/entertainment/web-series/panchayat-season-4-officially-announced-fans-excited-as-prime-video-announces-release-date-of-jitendra-kumars-cult-hit-101743671681626.html}}</ref>

